TEXT 160 0 Left 3 ;#197 Simple V-I curve tracer, as Alan draws it
TEXT 160 64 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WWY-pakm_OM
TEXT 160 112 Left 2 ;A triangle drives the part under test in series with a 10 ohm shunt. With the scope in X-Y
TEXT 160 144 Left 2 ;mode, the two channels draw the part's current against its voltage.
TEXT 1120 272 Left 2 !.tran 0 4m 0 1u
TEXT 1120 312 Left 2 !.meas tran VX_AT_PK FIND V(scope_x) AT 500u
TEXT 1120 352 Left 2 !.meas tran VY_AT_PK FIND V(scope_y) AT 500u
TEXT 1120 392 Left 2 !.meas tran VDUT_AT_PK FIND V(scope_x)-V(scope_y) AT 500u
TEXT 1120 432 Left 2 !.meas tran ID_AT_PK FIND I(D1) AT 500u
TEXT 160 640 Left 2 ;SCOPE_X and SCOPE_Y are the two scope inputs in Alan's drawing. His own note on the page
TEXT 160 672 Left 2 ;is that the method is not perfect, because the sense voltage read on Y is also part of X.
TEXT 160 720 Left 2 ;Alan drives the fixture from his scope's own AFG. Its menu at 5:00 reads Ramp, 1.0000 kHz,
TEXT 160 752 Left 2 ;2.0000 Vpp, 1.0000 V offset, so VGEN runs 0 to 2 V. He never names the part; 1N4148 is a choice.
